============================================================
## REQUEST FLOW IN DIFFERENT WEB APPLICATION ARCHITECTURES
============================================================

-------------------------------------------------------------
CASE 1: MONOLITHIC APPLICATION DEPLOYED ON A SINGLE SERVER
-------------------------------------------------------------

Suppose ek small monolithic application hai jo sirf ek single server par deployed hai.

Is case me DNS resolution ke baad directly us server ka IP return hota hai, aur saari requests usi ek server par jaati hain.

Flow:

    User
      |
      | DNS Resolution
      v
    DNS returns Server IP
      |
      v
    Single Server
      |
      v
    Monolithic Application processes the request


Ye setup small applications, personal projects, ya basic VPS deployments me common hai.



-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CASE 2: MONOLITHIC APPLICATION WITH MULTIPLE INSTANCES BEHIND A LOAD BALANCER
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Suppose ek monolithic application hai, lekin uske multiple instances 
different servers par run kar rahe hain. Kyunki ab ek se zyada servers hain,
to incoming traffic ko un servers ke beech distribute karne ke liye ek Load Balancer configure kiya jaata hai.


Is case me DNS resolution ke baad Load Balancer ka IP return hota hai.
URL routing usually application ke andar hoti hai, like Spring Boot controllers.

Example in Spring Boot:

    /users      -> UserController
    /orders     -> OrderController
    /payments   -> PaymentController

Flow:

    User
      |
      v
    DNS
      |
      | returns Load Balancer IP
      v
    Load Balancer
      |
      |------------------|------------------|
      v                  v                  v
    App Instance 1     App Instance 2     App Instance 3





