CASE 6: MONOLITHIC ARCHITECTURE WITH CDN AND LOAD BALANCER
--------------------------------------------------------------

Suppose ek monolithic application hai.

Uske multiple instances different servers par run kar rahe hain.
In instances ke traffic ko distribute karne ke liye ek Load Balancer hai.

CDN bhi present hai.

Is case me DNS resolution ke baad CDN ka IP return hota hai.

Flow:

                    User
                      |
                      v
                     DNS
                      |
                      | returns CDN IP
                      v
               Nearby CDN Edge
                      |
          -----------------------------
          |                           |
          | Cache Hit                 | Cache Miss
          |                           |
          |                           v
          |                     Load Balancer
          |                           |
          |          -----------------------------------
          |          |                 |               |
          |          v                 v               v
          |     Monolith-1       Monolith-2      Monolith-3
          |
          |
          +-----------------------------> Response returned directly from CDN


Explanation:

    Load Balancer incoming requests ko monolithic application ke multiple running instances ke beech distribute karta hai.

    Agar koi ek instance down ho jaye, to Load Balancer remaining healthy instances ko traffic forward kar sakta hai.

    URL routing application ke andar hoti hai.


## NOTE :
---------

Unlike a microservices architecture,
all business modules (Users, Orders, Payments, etc.)
are part of the same application deployment.

Although multiple instances of the application
may be running, every instance contains
the complete application.


Example in Spring Boot:

Saare endpoints same monolithic application
ke different controllers/modules ke through
handle kiye jaate hain.

Example:

    /users      -> UserController

    /orders     -> OrderController

    /payments   -> PaymentController

